WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:06.120
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:12.230
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:17.800
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:26.570
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.320
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.790
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:39.660
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:44.390
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.060
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.740
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.400
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.780
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.330
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.560
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:32.670
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.410
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:42.150
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:52.980
<i>The incident began when
Imazato-sensei was murdered on campus.</i>

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:53.950
<i>Just before his death,</i>

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.610
<i>Imazato-sensei apparently
said this to Narumi-san...</i>

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:01.130
<i>"I want to talk to you about
the Blade Chidlren."</i>

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.890
<i>Because he said these words,</i>

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:06.830
<i>someone took Imazato-sensei's life...</i>

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:09.400
<i>And then Narumi-san stood
up and took action.</i>

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.740
<i>"With your abilities, how many
suspects can you narrow it down to</i>

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.740
<i>with what little data we have?"</i>

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.840
<i> "Give me three days and I'll
have it under 20 people!"</i>

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:17.640
<i>"I'm counting on you."</i>

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:24.310
<i>Little did we suspect that things were
about to take such a drastic turn...</i>

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:37.020
Stay with me! Come on!

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.760
"Blind Spot in the Snare Net"

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.030
"Newspaper Office"

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:01.110
<i>The story began a little while back...</i>

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.520
<i>To meet Narumi-san's expectations,</i>

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:07.190
<i>I devoted myself to narrowing
down the list of people</i>

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:09.020
<i>who could have killed Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.430
<i>Your handmade sandwiches
are too yummy, Narumi-san!</i>

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:24.070
The egg and the mustard and
the mayonnaise are all amazing!

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.810
I'm so moved!

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.080
Your Chinese-style box lunch
the other day was great too,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.680
but today's egg sandwich is on
a completely different level!

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.820
One bite and I can instantly
feel the love you put into it!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.910
Eating this makes me
so unbelievably happy!

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.400
<i>That reminds me, Narumi-san.</i>

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.430
Even if we do narrow it down
to less than 10 suspects,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.040
how do you plan to identify
the killer after that?

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.570
Actually, I heard something
strange from that Wataya detective.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.640
Something strange?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.650
Remember that recent murder at
Sayoko Shiranagatani's home?

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.880
Yes...

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.720
Apparently Madoka's been investigating
that Sayoko girl ever since.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:13.920
She managed to get some information
about the Blade Children

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.980
from the house's owner.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.330
What kind of information?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:23.800
Apparently Sayoko's mother
said this before she died,

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.800
but it seems the Blade Children all
share a common physical characteristic.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.170
Physical characteristic?

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:34.240
They...The Blade Children, that is,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.410
have no 7th right rib.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.690
We, the Blade Children, have a
mark. We're each missing a rib.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.120
Don't worry about it.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.960
They still haven't caught
wind of that fact yet.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.960
<i>You underestimate too much, Kosuke-kun.</i>

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.630
That detective lady is all
over Sayoko Shiranagatani.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.570
We should assume she's found out
and put ourselves on standby...

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.900
...or else Little Narumi will catch us.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.100
The head Shiranagatani
apparently doesn't believe it,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.070
but in actuality, Sayoko is missing a rib.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:05.510
"Imazato"

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.910
<i>"Imazato"
So then the X-ray picture
in Imazato-sensei's locker</i>

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.050
<i>So then the X-ray picture
in Imazato-sensei's locker</i>

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.310
is connected to that!

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.480
I thought it was odd when I saw it

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.090
among the documents the police seized.

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.190
<i>Imazato-sensei was eliminated
because he was involved</i>

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.820
with the Blade Children, wasn't he?

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.930
At any rate, we're going to
narrow down the list of suspects

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.000
and then check those suspects' ribs.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.200
The killer is already in the net.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.630
We've won.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.400
No, we haven't lost.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.010
There's a way to turn the tables.

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:37.270
How so?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:40.910
I'm the only one who fulfills
the killer's characteristics

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.210
that he listed.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.280
Sooner or later the snare
net will be completed

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.020
and there'll be no place to run.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.850
No, the net isn't complete yet.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:52.320
And it's that girl who's
actually laying the net out...

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.560
Yes...

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.960
We just need to eliminate the girl...

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.690
<i>The snare net is getting closer and
closer to completion, Narumi-san!</i>

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:11.980
<i>Narumi-san, Madoka-san's
dinner is important,</i>

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.780
but can't you pay a little
attention to me too?!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.250
We're investigating in plain
view for everyone to see,

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.980
so more and more information
is coming in, isn't it?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.390
Yes, but we're being so conspicuous

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:27.320
that the killer might run away from school.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.930
No, this killer won't run away.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.260
Why not?

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.660
Judging from the method
used to kill Imazato,

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:37.600
the killer is obviously someone
pretty confident in their abilities.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:39.340
When they see our snare net,

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.960
running away will be the
last thing they think of.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.140
What?

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:50.810
Nothing, it's just that
they'll come at us head on.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.650
Okay...

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.980
I know you, Rio.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.450
You plan to kill on
campus again, don't you?

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.290
To challenge Little Narumi.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:02.890
I have to challenge him head on.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:07.530
But he's guarding the girl
very closely at school.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.770
You'll have almost no
chance of getting at her.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:10.970
Yeah...

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.440
Maybe a trap, then...

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.570
Trap?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.770
I'll set up a deadly trap in a place

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:19.540
where I know she'll have
to go and directly touch.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.380
Can you take care of her
with any certainty that way?

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.810
I have a trump card.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.490
Come to think of it, you were the one

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.540
who made that bomb the other day, huh?

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:36.260
Assistant Inspector! Have you heard?

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.130
It seems your brother-in-law's
poking his head

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:40.330
into our investigations again!

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.330
Ayumu is?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.900
<i>Specifically, the case in which that
teacher, Imazato-san, was murdered.</i>

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.540
<i>Sonobe was involved with
Shiranagatani-san's case so I understand,</i>

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.300
but things look bad this time!

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.640
<i>What could Ayumu be trying
to do by himself?</i>

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.320
Let's call it a day.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.250
Alright...

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.580
I'll take you home.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:07.160
Is it that surprising?

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:07.360
Is it that surprising?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.790
But, but...

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.560
But what?

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.630
You're so cold of a person

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.730
that I never expected you
to say anything like that!

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.170
The reason is simple.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:19.600
What is it?

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.630
The killer is going to
try to get rid of you.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:27.240
The killer should be
planning to get rid of you

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:29.850
before the snare net is completed.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.580
In other words, they're
going to come after you

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.020
sometime today or tomorrow.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:36.590
Could you please not talk
about it so casually?

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.720
But it's okay.

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.860
Just as I said earlier, the
killer is full of confidence.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.990
If they're going to target you

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:44.390
then they'll do it on
campus with me nearby.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:47.200
So then why are you walking me home?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.370
We have to give the killer
a chance to set up the trap.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:53.300
Just trust me.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:58.110
Besides, I was counting
on them to target you.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:02.750
So I've tried to prevent the killer
from having an opportunity to kill you.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.780
I even made sure that no poison
was slipped into your food.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.220
So that's what those sandwiches were for?

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:12.660
I've asked you to do some dangerous work.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.890
It's my duty to protect you.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:18.560
Then you should've told me
that from the very start.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.500
But that doesn't change the
fact that you're a target.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.440
Listen, there are currently two
ways they might come after you.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.040
One is by shooting you
from a long distance.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.840
Shooting?!

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.640
But in spatial terms, an on-campus
shooting would be difficult.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.780
In which case the only other option

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.310
is that they will set up a mechanical trap.

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:39.410
A trap?!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.650
The newspaper office area
will be the location.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:45.490
<i>-And judging from the
incident the other day,
-Narumi-san!</i>

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:48.060
The trap will undoubtedly be a bomb.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.860
A bomb?!

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.260
Don't worry.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.370
We've always had a contingency
snare net in place.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.270
It'll drive them completely
out into the open.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.070
<i>Even though it first began with logic,</i>

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:08.550
<i>Narumi-san's judgment soon
reached a level beyond reasoning.</i>

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.550
What're you doing? Hurry up.

00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:13.450
Wait for me!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:20.990
That means you turned me into
a decoy without my permission!

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.990
Hiyono Double Punch!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:28.360
Bear! Bear! Bunny! Bunny!

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.400
<i>But there is one other unthinkable way</i>

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:34.000
<i>to break through the snare net...</i>

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:39.040
<i>Though realistically-speaking,
it's highly unlikely...</i>

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.630
Ow!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.650
All done!

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.480
It's so cute!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.190
Lemme see.

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:55.680
See? Isn't it cute?

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.260
<i>You call this cute?</i>

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:00.300
Hmph! You can't look at it anymore!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.930
Then I'll never know if it's cute or not.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.200
It's obviously cute!

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.510
Is that a Tasmanian Devil?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:09.440
Get out.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.520
I'll come with you if you're
on your way to set that bomb.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.420
You're so dumb.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:27.620
You know I'd never do that.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:33.160
Little Narumi is expecting
me to put this in the room.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:35.630
They don't hide their actions

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.500
and they even announced their deadline.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.700
All to trick us into thinking we need
to get rid of that newspaper girl.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.410
You can't be serious!

00:11:43.410 --> 00:11:45.710
<i>He's Kiyotaka-sama's brother.</i>

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.240
His reasoning is almost supernatural,

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.250
and he can tell what we're thinking.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.550
Naturally, he must've
seen through my actions

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:54.450
and put a contingency snare net in place.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.650
So now what? There's no way out!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.320
Don't worry.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.290
I'll be the one who wins.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:06.550
<i>See you later, Kosuke-kun.</i>

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.680
<i>Thanks, Kosuke-kun...</i>

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:25.010
You sure you'll be alright?

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.380
I'll be fine.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:30.350
After all, there's a place where
Little Narumi still can't tread.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.890
A place he still can't tread?

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:32.690
Yes.

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.960
The territory in which there
is no guarantee of safety

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.400
and only the ability to believe
in oneself will decide the victor.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.760
Hey now, what're you talking about?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.160
Okay, let's go home now!

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.550
Um, can I ask you one other thing?

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:56.710
What?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.780
Why are you pursuing the
mystery of the Blade Children?

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.520
Because it's the only clue to
finding my brother right now.

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:07.320
So why are you searching for your brother?

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.360
Well, he's my brother.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.330
With him gone, I can't help but worry.

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:14.000
Are you so sure?

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.330
You should know very well

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.670
<i>how amazing your brother is, Narumi-san.</i>

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:20.800
He's not the kind of person
to lose to anything.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.670
Even if you don't go after him he'll
show up safely sooner or later.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:28.010
In fact, you might be getting
in his way by going after him.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.910
You must feel that in your heart.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:35.250
<i>Isn't Madoka-san actually
the one you're worrying about?</i>

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:46.730
My brother disappeared less
than a year after they married.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:48.530
For two long years,

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.190
she's desperately searched for him.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.610
Well, the train's here.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:35.550
I'll see you home...

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:37.310
I'll be fine now.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:52.960
Outside the window, kira kira kira ri

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:59.560
A shooting star streaks

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:04.530
I'm back.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.880
Huh? You're home pretty early today.

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.580
I came home so hungry!

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.980
Are you trying to starve me to death?

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:16.150
You're not a kid, you
could've eaten before me.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:21.260
You're sticking your head
into more incidents, I hear?

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:23.490
What are you scheming this time?

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:25.760
I'm not scheming anything.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:28.460
And anyway, food comes first.

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:34.100
Outside the window, kira kira kira ri

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:35.870
What a weird song.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.040
Please, Ayumu.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.710
Stop butting in.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:44.880
I've been meaning to tell
you this for a while...

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.280
Have you been getting a
little fatter lately?

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:51.750
Now that I think about it, your pants
have strangely grown a bit in size,

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.960
which would also explain why
the food in the refrigerator

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:56.390
has started to disappear abnormally.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:59.520
Oh, really?

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.600
He evaded it again...

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:18.080
<i>And so the night before the third
and final day wore on for each of us.</i>

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.480
<i>Just then, rain fell,</i>

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:23.040
<i>almost as if it felt sympathy
for the tragedy about to occur...</i>

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.930
Is there really a trap in this room?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:38.270
Nothing seems out of
place from yesterday...

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:40.500
That area's the most suspicious.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.270
Though I don't think
we're up against someone

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.280
who would set up such a simple trap.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.970
Make up your mind!

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:03.090
<i>Narumi-san, school's almost out.</i>

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:06.160
Do you think maybe
nothing's going to happen?

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.530
Good question.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.300
Um...

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.470
This is the room for the
school paper, right?

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.270
Oh, it's you...

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.910
Can we help you?

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.580
Well, I found this in a
hallway on the first floor.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:30.090
This was taped to the kitty's head...

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.260
"Take me to the Newspaper Office"

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:34.360
<i>Don't tell me there's a bomb inside it?!</i>

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.160
<i>Wait!</i>

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.660
<i>At that size, its explosive
power is limited!</i>

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:41.720
<i>Plus there's no way to reliably
kill the target this way!</i>

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:46.800
Huh? There's a ticking
sound inside the kitty...

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:47.730
Hey, now!

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.300
Are you insane?!

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.100
Destroying your own chest
with a bomb like that!

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:17.970
But that's the only way to
make it impossible to determine

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:19.240
if I have the rib or not.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:20.570
But still!

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:23.770
It won't be so strong that
I'll die on the spot.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:26.110
Just enough to lose a couple ribs.

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:28.240
I won't die as long as I'm lucky.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:29.780
You can't be serious about this!

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.910
The risk of dying is too high!

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:33.120
Think about it.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:36.850
Little Narumi's snare net relies
on the lack of a single rib.

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:40.390
By making that distinction
impossible, the net can be cut.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.390
What's the point of escaping the snare net

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.990
if you wind up dead?!

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:48.360
That's the reason why it's so effective.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.270
There's a lot to be gained
by winning this gamble.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:56.360
Did you have this all figured
out from the very start?

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:01.340
I believe in my luck and ability.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:04.870
I will always come back,
even from the abyss of death.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:12.890
<i>What on earth did I misread?!</i>

00:19:12.890 --> 00:19:15.760
<i>Calm down! Reform your logic!</i>

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.660
<i>Nothing's over yet!</i>

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:29.670
<i>And thus the incident ended in
a way we had never anticipated.</i>

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:35.310
<i>Rio Takeuchi-san suffered severe
trauma from her left chest to her side,</i>

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:37.400
<i>and is hospitalized even still.</i>

00:19:38.180 --> 00:19:39.520
<i>As for Narumi-san,</i>

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:42.220
<i>he didn't say a thing during
the police questioning</i>

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.080
<i>and is always lost deep in thought.</i>

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:47.490
<i>If only he would stop
worrying about it by himself</i>

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.220
<i>and tell me about it...</i>

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.390
<i>Narumi-san.</i>

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.930
Could you tell me what you're
thinking about already?

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.940
<i>We got the innocent Takeuchi-san involved</i>

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.540
because of what we were doing, you know!

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:05.880
She's not innocent at all.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:12.520
<i>I had realized there was that
way to escape our snare net...</i>

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:16.320
But I figured blowing herself
up was just too dangerous!

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.490
Wait!

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:21.760
You're saying she blew
her chest up on purpose?!

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.460
If she planned to kill you,

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:26.300
then she wouldn't have
used such a weak bomb.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:31.100
<i>She's the Blade Child who
killed Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:32.840
No way!

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:36.010
Three weeks have passed since the incident.

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:39.680
She probably believes she's gotten
away and has let her guard down!

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:41.310
I refuse to give up now!

00:20:41.310 --> 00:20:43.010
I'll get her!

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:51.920
<i>Narumi-san seems very
different this time around.</i>

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:54.480
<i>He's usually much more composed.</i>

00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:04.620
<i>Little Brother, let us begin
our non-rigged last game...</i>

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:10.670
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:17.370
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:35.530
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:41.170
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:47.070
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:53.650
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:59.380
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:04.590
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:10.430
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:22.040
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:27.810
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:34.120
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.770
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:43.350
Beautiful flowers have thorns!

00:22:43.350 --> 00:22:44.750
There is luck in the last helping.

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:46.180
Where there's a front, there's a back!

00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:47.790
Delicious blowfish has poison!

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:50.520
<i>But for some reason Narumi-san's
normal composure is gone!</i>

00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:52.520
Have more confidence!

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.030
<i>Next episode's highlights include
Narumi-san's special piano skills</i>

00:22:55.030 --> 00:22:57.430
<i>and a daikon-peeling, tightrope-walking act!</i>

00:22:57.430 --> 00:22:59.530
Eh? No lifelines?!

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:01.800
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:01.800 --> 00:23:03.400
The Non-Believer's Choice

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:05.430
That's all for today's Hiyono's Playhouse!
